1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,605
A wheel of magnets.

2
00:00:02,625 --> 00:00:05,105
No fuel. No plug.

3
00:00:05,125 --> 00:00:07,128
It never stops.

4
00:00:07,375 --> 00:00:12,605
1269. A French army besieges Lucera, in Italy.

5
00:00:12,625 --> 00:00:17,980
One of its engineers, Peter Peregrinus, writes a letter about magnets.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,195
In it: a wheel that magnets would drive around forever.

7
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:27,730
In the 1600s, English scholar John Wilkins describes a ramp.

8
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:31,605
A magnet at the top pulls an iron ball up.

9
00:00:31,625 --> 00:00:36,187
It drops through a hole, rolls back down, and climbs again.

10
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:41,355
1775. The Paris Academy of Sciences

11
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:45,230
says it will no longer deal with perpetual motion.

12
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:50,181
Today, the U.S. patent office can demand a working model.

13
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:53,855
So why does every magnet wheel stop?

14
00:00:53,875 --> 00:00:56,480
A magnet's pull is a hill.

15
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:00,480
Every bit of help going in is paid back coming out.

16
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:03,855
Over one full turn, the sum is zero.

17
00:01:03,875 --> 00:01:08,308
Friction takes the rest, and the wheel parks at its sticky point.

18
00:01:08,625 --> 00:01:13,237
Lodestone asks: what if the sticky point could be switched off?

19
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:17,700
24 magnets on a 1.2 m rotor.

20
00:01:17,875 --> 00:01:20,480
Trial one. Bare magnets.

21
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:23,000
3 turns. Stopped.

22
00:01:23,125 --> 00:01:27,105
Trial two. A shield slides over the sticky point.

23
00:01:27,125 --> 00:01:32,093
11 turns. Stopped. Moving the shield costs what it saves.

24
00:01:32,250 --> 00:01:37,605
Trial three. A coil fires at the sticky point and cancels the pull.

25
00:01:37,625 --> 00:01:40,281
40 days. Still turning.

26
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:42,300
One catch.

27
00:01:42,375 --> 00:01:45,271
The coil runs on a battery.

28
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:47,980
Lodestone is cleared.

29
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,247
As an electric motor.

30
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:54,230
Peregrinus wanted a wheel that never stops.

31
00:01:54,250 --> 00:01:57,066
We built one. It has a plug.
